WEBVTT

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:09.330
Note: Bentora is a made-up word that's supposed 
to mean "spaceship" in an alien language.

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:06.220
Bentora, bentora, space people!

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:09.340
Bentora, bentora, space people!

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.990
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:14.650
What, no "shugo, shugo" today?

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.020
Just watch today's episode, and you'll see why.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.350
So if you're curious...

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.110
But even if you're not...

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:23.690
Don't change that channel!

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.710
Doki!

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.530
Yes! Yes!

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.400
Let's go!

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.520
Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:43.280
Shugo, shugo! Yes!

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.850
Swing your arms! Hop, step, jump!

00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:51.440
Now start marching straight ahead!

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.110
Way too awesome! Yes!

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:58.770
Every dream I've ever had!

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:04.680
Since they're all actually coming true.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:10.670
What kind of person will I be today?

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:15.730
What counts is being true to yourself!

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:19.610
Going somewhere?

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:22.010
Take it to the finish!

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:25.510
You'll always be able to

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:28.390
unlock your heart.

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:31.340
So keep on changing!

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.680
It's so exciting!

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:41.890
Let's go forward, believing in our hearts!

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.950
Straight ahead!

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:46.890
Yeah! Yeah!

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.730
Ikuto...

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.150
Your sleeping face is even more adorable than I imagined.

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.350
It was just a dream...

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.780
What's wrong with Amu-chan?

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.990
Perhaps she had a peculiar dream...

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:28.890
Good morning, Amu-chan!

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.500
Time to rise and shine!

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.130
Yeah, I'm up, I'm shining.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.130
Really?

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:37.590
I swear! Now, about that breakfast...

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.170
I wonder what Mom'll put in my lunch today.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.900
Yeah, something ain't right...

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:53.340
Could she be worried because Ikuto isn't here anymore?

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:59.200
Episode 67
A UFO Girl Appears!

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:02.930
Let's begin our meeting.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:06.270
On today's agenda, we'll be discussing 
the club activities reports and—

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.550
Tadase.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.400
Hinamori-san?

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.680
Amu-chi!

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:16.300
Something on your mind?

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.440
You're acting weird today.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.690
You were on another planet in class.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.700
It looks like something's really troubling you.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:26.550
Why don't you tell us about it, if it would help?

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:30.810
Should I? But I can't tell them 
Ikuto's been staying at my house...

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:37.620
Um... there's this cat! A stray cat showed up at our house! Right?

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:38.890
A cat?

00:03:38.890 --> 00:03:40.480
Right, right! A cat!

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.610
It hung around for a bit and then, poof, took off.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.360
It just kind of threw me for a loop is all...

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.440
This is all over a cat?

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:52.180
I'd feel the same, though. Cats can be so fickle, you know?

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:56.360
We really should begin our meeting now.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:59.150
What a narrow escape!

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:03.290
Someone must be talking about us.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.190
Easter's goons-nya...

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:12.980
We're not safe here-nya!

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.430
Ikuto, we've gotta move-nya!

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:17.710
Yeah.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.110
Giant UFO Crash Sighting!

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:25.710
Let's cut to the crash site footage.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:31.540
What are your thoughts on the UFO 
recently discovered in Brazil?

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:34.710
A real UFO? Well, it's incredible!

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.650
Poppycock! It's nothing but plasma, I say!

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:40.660
Oh? You don't believe it's there, Professor?

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:44.810
Perhaps only those who believe 
wholeheartedly in UFOs can see it?

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:47.610
Neat! UFOs are cool!

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:50.670
Aliens have definitely come to Earth... probably.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:54.000
Do you believe they exist, Amu-chan?

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.520
Sure, I guess...

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:01.500
That there's a UFO!

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.430
It came all crashin' to Earth like, 
bam! Ain't that right, Lulu?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:06.880
The whole thing irritates me.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:10.770
I'm heading out.

00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:12.600
Hey, wait up, y'hear!

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.430
Well, picking up the vibes of any lost children?

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:24.320
Do you believe in UFOs, Lulu?

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.900
Huh? The mere idea is ludicrous.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:29.060
You ain't a dreamer, are ya?

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:32.100
I might not believe in UFOs, but I still have dreams.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.040
Oh? And what would they be?

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.450
That's...

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:38.570
Well now, guess you can't find 'em, huh?

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:43.090
You can't find your own dreams anywhere!

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:45.420
You can't find your—

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.200
Nana!

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:49.390
You ain't gettin' away with this!

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.450
There's your Nagoya accent!

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.790
Be quiet...

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.720
Oh, I've got it!

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.480
We've just gotta herd up a lotta folks.

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:00.170
Leave that there all to me!

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.970
What's got everyone so excited?

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.220
Big news, guys! Big news!

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.340
Someone found a crop circle near the riverbed!

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:14.380
Dechu!

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:17.230
A crop circle? Really?

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:21.090
You mean one of those circle things UFOs make in the ground?

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.760
Exactly!

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.680
Let's go check it out after school!

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:26.230
Yeah!

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.600
All right, let's hustle!

00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:42.340
Bit small, don't you think?

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:45.260
That must be one tiny alien...

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:48.680
Actually, aliens come in a wide variety of sizes.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:52.010
From the most minuscule, to those comparable 
to Guardian Characters...

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:54.680
Some even reach three meters in height.

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:58.160
You sure know your stuff.

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:01.210
I've been interested in UFOs since I was a boy.

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:05.300
Once we achieve world domination, 
we'll set our sights on the universe itself!

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.580
I don't think they even exist.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:10.690
Huh? But it'd be pretty funny if they did!

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:12.400
Isn't it a little lopsided?

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:13.530
Yeah...

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:16.010
Even we could make that-dechu.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:20.960
Those jerks, makin' fun of the masterpiece 
I struggled so hard to create!

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.330
Let's go, Nana.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:27.050
But why would aliens do something like this?

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.750
Don't they often represent a message?

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:30.580
Yeah.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:35.070
I wonder where UFOs come from, and where they're going...

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:39.350
Maybe they're just aimlessly wandering the universe.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:40.960
Aimlessly wandering...

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:52.620
We gathered a lot of people together, 
but none of them were lost.

00:07:52.620 --> 00:07:55.220
Well, no need to get your feathers 
in a bunch, we'll find one.

00:07:55.430 --> 00:08:01.330
But we're on a mission to get the Embryo 
before Easter finds it with Ikuto's violin!

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.140
We don't have any time to waste!

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:05.140
I hear ya...

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:09.030
We'll find that there Embryo so we can help your mama-san!

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:14.860
Exactly. I need to help my mother star in 
an acclaimed film that'll go down in history.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:23.560
Hey, Lulu, if you could have the Embryo 
grant a second wish, what would it be?

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:26.100
Well...

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:29.110
You never change, Lulu.

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:31.530
So bashful about your own dreams...

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:35.710
If y'all want your dreams to come true, you'd 
better think clearly and carefully about 'em.

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.610
That's enough preaching from you.

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:38.860
Fine, fine.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:41.830
Bentora, bentora, space people!

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:42.770
What's that?

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:46.100
Bentora, bentora, space people!

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:49.890
Oh Great UFO, creator of this crop circle, please respond!

00:08:50.090 --> 00:08:53.460
Bentora, bentora, space people!

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:53.450
Look, this is all your fault.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:56.290
Who's there?

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:01.780
Are you calling the UFO as well?

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:02.880
UFO?

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:08.430
If you say that chant with all your heart, the 
UFO will sense it telepathically and come here!

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:10.540
You... believe in them?

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:15.060
Of course! I saw one once when I was a little kid.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:17.360
It was flitting around the sky at sunset.

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:21.740
Ever since then, it's been my dream 
to make contact with a UFO.

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:25.100
So you're one of those first contact people...

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:27.680
Right! You do know them!

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:29.980
It's just what I heard on TV.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:34.600
But it makes me so happy that you 
at least know a little bit about UFOs.

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:38.380
This here's one interesting kid...

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:40.360
You think?

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:42.620
I'm Kusanagi Nayuta.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:43.780
Nayuta?

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:46.810
Yeah, my dad chose my name.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:51.060
It's of Indian origin, and it means one hundred billion.

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:56.460
But you know, space has way more stars than that.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:02.360
I'm sure that somewhere out there is another planet 
with a civilization more advanced than Earth's.

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:05.860
It wouldn't be strange at all for a UFO 
to come from someplace like that.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:06.960
Don't you think?

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:09.590
You might be right.

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:11.790
What's your name?

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:14.590
Lulu. Lulu De Morcerf.

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:20.400
I think that girl'd be a good target for a ? Egg!

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.820
I'm not so sure...

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.730
She didn't give me the impression that she's lost.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:32.650
Oh, be honest! You just wanna be her friend, right?

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:35.360
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:10:35.360 --> 00:10:36.320
Let's go.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:40.130
Bentora, bentora, space people!

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:41.760
Cut it out already...

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:57.810
Let's just go back to Amu's house, Ikuto.

00:10:57.810 --> 00:11:00.380
You're really weak-nya.

00:11:00.380 --> 00:11:03.030
I just need to sleep it off.

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:04.460
But...

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:11.150
Let me rest here for a bit.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:12.320
Sure...

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.190
Good morning!

00:11:41.190 --> 00:11:43.090
What is it, Amu-chan?

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:46.050
You sure are up bright and early today.

00:11:46.050 --> 00:11:50.010
Yeah! I've decided not to worry about that guy anymore.

00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:53.600
Our old Amu-chan has come back to us.

00:11:54.930 --> 00:11:57.650
Amu-chan, what the heck was that?!

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.400
What? You mean this?

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:08.130
The crop circle seems to have 
been merely a prank.

00:12:08.130 --> 00:12:09.820
Obviously...

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:12.130
Man... so lame.

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:15.460
How neat would it have been had it been authentic?

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:18.380
Cheer up, you two.

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:22.860
There's a chance UFOs and aliens exist. 
It's better to keep the dream alive!

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:27.720
Hinamori-san... I'm glad to 
see you're feeling better.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:33.140
She's right. Guardian Characters look like 
aliens to normal people, after all.

00:12:34.010 --> 00:12:36.680
We're not aliens!

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:39.600
We are not Greys!

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:42.840
Greys are aliens who have faces like this-dechu.

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:44.380
Hello!

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:47.240
That makes so much sense! Guardian Characters are aliens!

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.310
No, we're not!

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:55.480
Rima, don't laugh!

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:07.470
That crop circle yesterday was just someone's prank.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:11.050
Well, duh. You actually believed it was for real?

00:13:13.950 --> 00:13:17.580
UFOs exist... I just know it.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:21.040
I'm home!

00:13:21.040 --> 00:13:22.890
It went a little later than I expected.

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:25.090
Welcome home, Maman.

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:28.430
You look tired.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:31.220
Television is a lot like a festival.

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:36.080
You live it up as much as you can, but it's over in a flash.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.800
But that's what makes it fun, you know?

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:43.770
Maman looked tired...

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:46.810
It's proof that she doesn't belong in television.

00:13:46.810 --> 00:13:50.180
Well then, we've gotta hurry up and find the Embryo.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.790
I'm sensing someone who feels lost!

00:13:54.790 --> 00:13:56.560
Lead me to them, Nana.

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:02.930
I think it's coming from this direction.

00:14:03.160 --> 00:14:04.940
Thank you, come again.

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.150
I found her!

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:09.720
Oh, Lulu-chan!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.440
And this is <i>UFO World.</i>

00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:20.230
It has information about UFOs from around 
the world! Amazing, don't you think?

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:21.620
Sure...

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:23.680
Lulu, what's the hold up?

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:26.960
She seems happy on the outside, but 
her poor little heart's shoutin' at me!

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:30.180
Oh yeah, do you know about cattle mutilation?

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:32.640
Cattle... what?

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:38.090
Livestock are abducted and taken aboard a UFO...

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:41.090
Then they get dumped with their 
stomachs mysteriously cut open...

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:45.600
When <i>that</i> happens, there's always a UFO sighting.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:47.000
What... the heck?

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:49.510
Oh, do you know about implants?

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:56.080
They're the strange objects aliens insert 
into your body after they abduct you.

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:01.260
Why would they do that?

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:05.770
I've read that the implant allows you 
to freely communicate with the UFO!

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.880
I wished they'd do it to me!

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:11.940
Yup, you're <i>different</i>, all right.

00:15:11.940 --> 00:15:13.470
But...

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:19.600
I heard that the crop circle yesterday was a fake.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:21.590
That not true... right?

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.000
Lulu, now's your chance!

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:29.160
What're ya hesitatin' for? Think of your mama-san!

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:36.480
You're lost, aren't you?

00:15:37.770 --> 00:15:42.000
You want everyone to believe in UFOs.

00:15:43.090 --> 00:15:47.370
This jewelry will grant that wish.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:59.140
? Character Change.

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.610
Ah, Amu-chan!

00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:02.450
What is it, a ? Egg?

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:04.390
Yeah, and it's close!

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:10.960
Lulu, you've got to keep a look out for the Embryo!

00:16:10.960 --> 00:16:11.800
Right...

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:16.310
Her <i>again</i>?

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:18.560
What... is this?

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:22.490
Bentora, bentora, space people.

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:26.080
Bentora, bentora, space people.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:28.080
Are they doing a circle dance?

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:30.360
I doubt it.

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:31.310
Look!

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.850
That girl is the one with the ? Egg!

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:41.010
Hey!

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:43.450
What are you doing?

00:16:43.450 --> 00:16:45.050
Why are you chanting?

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:48.220
We're calling the UFOs.

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:50.380
UFOs?

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:54.990
I'm not an expert on this, but I don't 
think UFOs will come just by chanting.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:59.680
They only appear before people who 
believe in them with their whole hearts!

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:05.280
That's right! If you just force people 
to chant, the UFOs won't come.

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:09.320
Maybe they don't believe now, but 
they will after they see one!

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:13.390
I won't let anyone get in the way of my dream!

00:17:25.890 --> 00:17:28.990
Character Transformation: UFO Dream!

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:31.390
Ion Drive!

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:41.770
I'll make you all have a close encounter!

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:47.180
This is just wrong...

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:54.860
I can't let Easter get away with using 
people's dreams to catch the Embryo.

00:17:59.020 --> 00:18:00.650
My heart:

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:02.400
Unlock!

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.420
Character Transformation: Amulet Heart!

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:30.310
Heart Speeders!

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:38.850
Lulu, after 'em!

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:46.560
I'll make you all believe that UFOs exist!

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.160
A crop circle?

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.360
For real?

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:02.290
Now everyone will believe in them, right?

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:09.300
Get out of my way!

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:27.200
Hey!

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:28.910
Listen to—

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:31.460
What's that?

00:19:31.460 --> 00:19:32.360
A UFO?

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:33.400
Really?

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:38.260
Believe in UFOs, all of you!

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:49.210
Bentora, bentora, space people!

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:54.160
Bentora, bentora, space people...

00:19:54.160 --> 00:19:58.510
Bentora, bentora, space people...

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:01.740
Ran, switch with me!

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:03.010
Okay!

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:09.690
Character Transformation: Amulet Spade!

00:20:17.820 --> 00:20:21.010
Prism Music!

00:20:30.860 --> 00:20:34.730
Don't you think it's wrong to force 
others to share your beliefs?

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:38.090
As long as <i>you</i> believe, that should be enough!

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:43.750
Are you calling my dream stupid, too?!

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.960
It's not up to others to judge whether 
someone's dream is stupid or not.

00:20:46.960 --> 00:20:51.010
What's important is to chase your dream with 
everything you've got, no matter what it is.

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:56.750
No matter what my dream is... With all I've got...

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:04.090
Negative Heart: Lock On!

00:21:07.460 --> 00:21:09.460
Open Heart!

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:45.060
Huh? What was I...

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.850
Was I abducted by aliens?!

00:21:56.290 --> 00:22:00.360
I really hope I can contact a UFO someday.

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:06.310
"Chase your dream with everything 
you've got, no matter what it is."

00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:08.800
That girl says some darn right things now and then.

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:10.430
You think?

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:14.400
Another day with no Embryo...

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:17.320
Oh, can the act already.

00:22:25.200 --> 00:22:26.000
(For real?)

00:22:27.930 --> 00:22:28.300
(Eh?)

00:22:28.300 --> 00:22:31.010
Lotta love! Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:22:31.010 --> 00:22:33.670
Lotta love! Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:22:33.910 --> 00:22:38.850
If we ended up becoming adults today, {kyou mo}

00:22:38.850 --> 00:22:43.480
I bet we'd lose sight of everything except what's in front of us. {kitto}

00:22:43.480 --> 00:22:44.590
Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:49.750
So I wonder what we've been {kyoumade}

00:22:49.750 --> 00:22:54.130
so engrossed with finding all this time. {honto}

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:55.470
Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:22:55.470 --> 00:22:57.380
Someone once said: {dare ga}

00:22:57.380 --> 00:23:00.290
"We were born to be happy, {shiawase}

00:23:00.290 --> 00:23:06.550
so let's live to make others happy!" {soshite}

00:23:07.840 --> 00:23:09.030
How long will I have to {dore kurai}

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:10.730
carry all this love in my heart? {mune ippai}

00:23:10.730 --> 00:23:11.780
How long will I have to {dore kurai}

00:23:11.780 --> 00:23:13.400
carry all this love in my heart? {mune ippai}

00:23:13.400 --> 00:23:18.910
I wonder when I'll be able to let it all out. {kakaetara}

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:19.910
How many of {dore kurai}

00:23:19.910 --> 00:23:21.560
all those days in my heart... {mune ippai}

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:22.620
How many of{dore kurai}

00:23:22.620 --> 00:23:24.380
all those days in my heart... {mune ippai}

00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:29.790
How many of them have we run through? {ano hi}

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:30.840
With this much love {kore kurai}

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:32.530
filling my heart... {mune ippai}

00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:33.620
With this much love{kore kurai}

00:23:33.620 --> 00:23:35.200
filling my heart... {mune ippai}

00:23:35.200 --> 00:23:37.920
I hugged you tightly, {kimi wo}

00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:43.340
and during that time, we both felt so much happiness. {futari}

00:23:43.340 --> 00:23:45.640
Lotta love! Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:23:45.640 --> 00:23:46.140
(Why?)

00:23:46.140 --> 00:23:48.860
Lotta love! Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:23:48.860 --> 00:23:51.410
Lotta love! Lotta love! Lotta love!

00:23:51.410 --> 00:23:52.740
